Subject: SOP First Interrupt Resume Contract V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Interrupt Contract UUID: bb985c95-1b85-4e3b-a90b-60b33df54171

@ [slice_surface] docs/slices/FSC3_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [runtime_boundary] docs/runtime/FSC3_Runtime_Boundary_And_Invariant_Map.v1.sop
@ [graph_contract] docs/runtime/WholeFieldPlannerGraph_Contract.v1.sop
@ [planning_coordination_pack] docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
@ [operator_template] docs/operators/Operator_Contract_Template.v1.sop

& [SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1] is the FSC3 contract for runtime interrupt, handoff, and resume behavior
  + [contract_id] is sop-first-interrupt-resume-contract-v1
  + [contract_uuid] is bb985c95-1b85-4e3b-a90b-60b33df54171
  + [slice_id] is FSC3-S03
  + [authority_scope] is interrupt kind map, required context packet, human/deeper-model handoff, resume condition contract, no-hidden-mutation rule, and retry policy
  + [implementation_scope] is runtime interrupt contract only
  + [graph_dependency] is docs/runtime/WholeFieldPlannerGraph_Contract.v1.sop

  = must: pause graph mutation when runtime state exceeds accepted contract authority
  = must: preserve enough context for SOP-first reconsideration, SJS processing, human review, or deeper model judgment
  = must: resume only from accepted source, proof, decision, claim resolution, or human override records
  - never: implement interrupt handlers, UI prompts, transport, or runtime code in this contract

& [InterruptKindMap] is the interrupt kind map for WholeFieldPlannerGraph
  + [interrupt_kind] is ambiguous_identity
  + [interrupt_kind] is authority_conflict
  + [interrupt_kind] is stale_input
  + [interrupt_kind] is missing_proof_route
  + [interrupt_kind] is contested_coordination_claim
  + [interrupt_kind] is unsupported_scope
  + [interrupt_kind] is high_risk_operation
  + [interrupt_kind] is human_override_required
  + [interrupt_kind] is checkpoint_authority_confusion

  = must: classify any unknown authority-sensitive stop as sop_first_interrupt rather than success
  = must: preserve interrupt_kind in operator_trace and graph terminal state

& [InterruptContextPacket] is the required context carried out of a graph interrupt
  + [required_field] is interrupt_id
  + [required_field] is interrupt_kind
  + [required_field] is graph_state_ref
  + [required_field] is active_work_packet_ref
  + [required_field] is current_node_id
  + [required_field] is input_record_ref_set
  + [required_field] is output_record_ref_set
  + [required_field] is operator_trace_ref_set
  + [required_field] is checkpoint_ref
  + [required_field] is source_context_ref_set
  + [required_field] is authority_basis_ref_set
  + [required_field] is unresolved_question
  + [required_field] is mutation_blocked_set
  + [required_field] is required_resolution
  + [required_field] is stale_after

  = must: be sufficient for another conversation or model to reconstruct the reason for the pause
  = must: avoid embedding unreviewed source mutations as if they were authority

& [HandoffPolicy] is the policy for routing interrupt context to the right authority layer
  + [handoff_target] is SOP reconsideration for semantic ambiguity, authority conflict, unsupported scope, and missing proof route
  + [handoff_target] is SJS processing when a source specification or canonical authority must be reprocessed
  + [handoff_target] is human review for human_override_required and high_risk_operation
  + [handoff_target] is coordination review for contested_coordination_claim
  + [handoff_target] is freshness review for stale_input and checkpoint_authority_confusion

  = must: keep the original graph conversation identity and claimant context available during handoff
  = must: treat transport or UI carrier as projection only

& [ResumeConditionContract] is the accepted condition set required before a graph may resume
  + [resume_condition] is accepted source clarification for ambiguous_identity
  + [resume_condition] is accepted authority decision for authority_conflict
  + [resume_condition] is refreshed input or accepted stale handling for stale_input
  + [resume_condition] is proof_result or accepted blocked route for missing_proof_route
  + [resume_condition] is released, superseded, or accepted contested coordination claim resolution for contested_coordination_claim
  + [resume_condition] is accepted scope change or packet rebake for unsupported_scope
  + [resume_condition] is explicit human override plus authority notice for high_risk_operation
  + [resume_condition] is accepted checkpoint invalidation or refreshed checkpoint context for checkpoint_authority_confusion

  = must: require source_ref_set and lineage_edge_set for every resume decision
  = must: force completion_review_delta_gate when the resume condition changes packet, requirement, support, coordination, or model-route assumptions

& [NoHiddenMutationRule] is the no-hidden-mutation rule for interrupts and resumes
  + [blocked_mutation] is source specification edit
  + [blocked_mutation] is accepted boundary pack edit
  + [blocked_mutation] is canonical authority edit
  + [blocked_mutation] is checkpoint authority promotion
  + [blocked_mutation] is work packet scope expansion
  + [blocked_mutation] is coordination claim resolution
  + [blocked_mutation] is next gate opening

  = must: preserve attempted mutation as trace, support_gap, stale_projection, fault_record, or completion_review blocker
  = must: require explicit accepted authority before retry or resume

& [RetryAndResumePolicy] is the retry policy for graph terminal interrupt states
  + [retry_allowed_when] is interrupt context is accepted and still fresh
  + [retry_allowed_when] is required resolution record exists and is current
  + [retry_allowed_when] is checkpoint context is current or deliberately rebuilt from accepted records
  + [retry_forbidden_when] is accepted boundary pack changed without revalidation
  + [retry_forbidden_when] is work_packet is stale
  + [retry_forbidden_when] is coordination claim is contested
  + [retry_forbidden_when] is support_delta or requirement_delta requires rebake

  = must: retry through the graph contract path rather than jumping to a later node silently

& [InterruptResumeCoverageReview] is the FSC3-S03 coverage checklist
  + [interrupt_kind_map_present] is InterruptKindMap
  + [context_packet_present] is InterruptContextPacket
  + [handoff_policy_present] is HandoffPolicy
  + [resume_condition_contract_present] is ResumeConditionContract
  + [no_hidden_mutation_rule_present] is NoHiddenMutationRule
  + [retry_policy_present] is RetryAndResumePolicy
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime interrupt handler implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is UI prompt implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is transport implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control

  = must: reject FSC3-S03 if interrupt can resume without accepted resolution
  = must: open FSC3-S04 only after this contract is accepted by completion review
